1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,430
Another method we're going to talk about is

2
00:00:02,430 --> 00:00:06,060
Thinking Hats which was something devised by Edward de Bono.

3
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:10,890
Thinking Hats allows you to make sure that different perspectives are being discussed.

4
00:00:10,890 --> 00:00:14,550
It also really pushes people to being open and understanding

5
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:16,800
different perspectives since the likely have

6
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,620
to represent viewpoints that aren't their own.

7
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:22,860
Another benefit is that by going through this exercise

8
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,100
together as a team with everyone wearing the same hat at

9
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:30,120
the same time is that it's way less confrontational than if

10
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:34,560
each team member was assigned their own specific hat to wear during the exercise.

11
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:37,545
Let's walk through the six different hats.

12
00:00:37,545 --> 00:00:42,150
The first hat we're going to talk about is the blue hat which represents process.

13
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:45,185
This is really about structuring the conversation and

14
00:00:45,185 --> 00:00:48,920
aligning on how we're going to think about this problem.

15
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:52,670
This hat can also be used at the end to summarize

16
00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:56,930
the conversation and make sure that there's alignment across everyone who's involved.

17
00:00:56,930 --> 00:00:59,425
The white hat represents data.

18
00:00:59,425 --> 00:01:04,235
These are more like fact sharing or fact-finding types of questions.

19
00:01:04,235 --> 00:01:07,010
What do we know? What do we need to find out?

20
00:01:07,010 --> 00:01:11,300
There's no viewpoints that are expressed when you're wearing the white hat.

21
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:14,540
The yellow hat represents benefits.

22
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:20,750
This is when you get to talk about optimism for why a specific idea could be useful.

23
00:01:20,750 --> 00:01:25,640
You'll want to make sure that you have logical reasons when you're wearing this hat.

24
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:29,255
Conversely, there's the black hat which represents judgment.

25
00:01:29,255 --> 00:01:34,445
This is really about focusing on the challenges of specific ideas or what could go wrong.

26
00:01:34,445 --> 00:01:39,605
Again, you'll want to make sure that you have reasoning behind all of the arguments here.

27
00:01:39,605 --> 00:01:43,595
Then you have the green hat which represents creativity.

28
00:01:43,595 --> 00:01:47,175
These are things like new views, alternative solutions,

29
00:01:47,175 --> 00:01:51,035
ways that you can de-risk and overcome challenges.

30
00:01:51,035 --> 00:01:55,025
Lastly, you have the red hat which represents intuition.

31
00:01:55,025 --> 00:01:58,340
This is just about your gut feelings and hunches.

32
00:01:58,340 --> 00:02:01,205
There's no reasoning needed when you're wearing this hat.

33
00:02:01,205 --> 00:02:05,660
You can come up with different sequencing in terms of the order that you'll

34
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:10,510
wear hats based on the specific problem that you are trying to solve.

35
00:02:10,510 --> 00:02:12,680
You'll always want to start and end with

36
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:15,800
a blue hat though no matter what problem you're working on.

37
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:20,660
I found that there's a order that works really well for picking between

38
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:25,760
different ideas and we'll walk through what that process looks like.

39
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:29,225
We'll start with the blue hat which represents process.

40
00:02:29,225 --> 00:02:33,320
At this point, this is really about structuring the conversation

41
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:36,320
and aligning with the team in terms of

42
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:39,385
the order of the hats that you all wear as a group,

43
00:02:39,385 --> 00:02:41,620
as well as, discussing the goals or

44
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:44,390
the outcomes that you're hoping to have from this conversation

45
00:02:44,390 --> 00:02:47,030
which in this case will really just be a lining on

46
00:02:47,030 --> 00:02:50,360
a specific idea to move forward with during the rest of the spring.

47
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:53,845
Then, you'll switch to the white hat which represents data.

48
00:02:53,845 --> 00:02:57,740
This is the time when you can talk about things like what do you know,

49
00:02:57,740 --> 00:03:00,950
what are the types of information that you need or need to find out,

50
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:03,875
and when you're wearing this hat it's really important that you're not

51
00:03:03,875 --> 00:03:07,310
advocating for or against any specific idea.

52
00:03:07,310 --> 00:03:10,519
You're really just providing facts or asking

53
00:03:10,519 --> 00:03:13,970
questions in terms of trying to find out information that you need to know.

54
00:03:13,970 --> 00:03:17,450
Some types of facts or questions that you might have when you're wearing

55
00:03:17,450 --> 00:03:21,500
this hat could be how many customers will use this product?

56
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:23,465
Or what's the size of the problem?

57
00:03:23,465 --> 00:03:25,640
Or how often would users use this?

58
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:27,740
Or what's the impact for users?

59
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:29,615
What's the impact for the business?

60
00:03:29,615 --> 00:03:32,135
Those are just a few types of examples.

61
00:03:32,135 --> 00:03:35,855
Then you'll switch to the green hat which is about creativity.

62
00:03:35,855 --> 00:03:40,610
This is really trying to push and come up with some new views are

63
00:03:40,610 --> 00:03:45,395
alternative solutions or ways to de-risk and overcome challenges.

64
00:03:45,395 --> 00:03:47,990
The goal here is to really stretch your thinking.

65
00:03:47,990 --> 00:03:49,940
You can look at all the ideas that are being

66
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:52,715
discussed and use them as a jumping-off point.

67
00:03:52,715 --> 00:03:57,155
In a way, this is similar to challenging assumptions that we talked about earlier.

68
00:03:57,155 --> 00:04:03,080
Then you'll switch to the yellow hat which is all focused about benefits of the idea.

69
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:04,460
When you're wearing this hat,

70
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:06,170
you will want to make sure that you have

71
00:04:06,170 --> 00:04:09,380
specific reasoning for the arguments that you're making.

72
00:04:09,380 --> 00:04:14,125
But things that you could talk about here are what is the user benefit?

73
00:04:14,125 --> 00:04:15,975
How will this help users?

74
00:04:15,975 --> 00:04:17,730
Will it save them time?

75
00:04:17,730 --> 00:04:19,050
Will it save money?

76
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:22,850
Is there some other value that users would get out of this product?

77
00:04:22,850 --> 00:04:25,670
Then, you'll switch to the black hat which is

78
00:04:25,670 --> 00:04:29,180
the opposite of the yellow hat and focus on judgment.

79
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:34,580
So the focus here is really around challenges or identifying what could go wrong.

80
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:36,240
Again when you're wearing this hat,

81
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:37,820
you'll want to make sure that you have

82
00:04:37,820 --> 00:04:41,735
logical reasoning and rationale behind all your arguments.

83
00:04:41,735 --> 00:04:44,630
Some examples of things that you could discuss or

84
00:04:44,630 --> 00:04:47,900
advocate for when you're wearing this hat is that an idea

85
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:52,550
doesn't actually solve a specific user need or that it could be difficult or

86
00:04:52,550 --> 00:04:57,710
costly to build and that lots of things could go wrong trying to build out the idea.

87
00:04:57,710 --> 00:05:00,920
Then you'll switch to the red hat which is intuition,

88
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:04,475
and at this point, it's just your gut feelings and hunches.

89
00:05:04,475 --> 00:05:06,335
You don't need to have any reasoning,

90
00:05:06,335 --> 00:05:08,745
but you should go through and

91
00:05:08,745 --> 00:05:11,930
have a conversation around all of the different ideas that are

92
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:14,600
being considered and get a sense of what

93
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:17,690
everyone's thinking after wearing all the previous hats.

94
00:05:17,690 --> 00:05:21,710
Then lastly you'll switch back to the blue hat where you'll summarize

95
00:05:21,710 --> 00:05:27,660
the conversation and align on the specific idea that the group thinks is best.

